<p class="sst-lead">A thin SVD of the weighted, centered landmark matrix gives a <strong>polar decomposition</strong>
&mdash; the heart of the Separable Representation by Quadrature Decomposition (SRQD).</p>

<p>\[ \sqrt{W}\,\mathcal{T}[\bm{c}](\{s_i\}) = \widetilde{X}\,P,\qquad
\widetilde{X}=U V^{\top},\quad P = V\Sigma V^{\top}\in \mathcal{S}^2_{++}. \]</p>

<div class="sst-frag">
  <p>The two factors are the whole point:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>\([\widetilde{X}]\in \mathrm{Gr}(2,n)\) is <strong>undulation</strong> &mdash; shape with scale removed,</li>
    <li>\(P\in\mathcal{S}^2_{++}\) is generalized <strong>scale</strong> &mdash; anisotropic, rotation-free.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="sst-note">Drag the landmarks. The ellipse is \(P\) (scale); the right panel is the standardized
  undulation \(\widetilde{X}=XP^{-1}\). Stretching the shape moves \(P\) but barely touches \([\widetilde{X}]\).</p>
</div>
